  "articleBody": "Knowing when to re-seal your log home's interior logs isn't about marking a date on the calendar, but rather observing the signs of wear and tear. Unlike exterior logs that are constantly battling the elements, interior logs have a bit of an easier life, but they still need attention. You'll want to keep an eye out for a few key indicators. One of the most common signs is a noticeable loss of sheen. If your logs used to have a lovely luster and now look dull or faded, it's probably time for a fresh coat. Another good test is to see how water reacts with the surface. If water no longer beads up and instead soaks into the wood, that's a clear signal that the protective qualities of your sealer are diminishing. Over time, friction and daily activities can also cause the finish to thin or wear away in high-traffic areas. Regular cleaning and dusting are great, but eventually, the protective layer will need to be renewed. If you're unsure, or if you notice any areas of concern, it's a good idea to consult with professionals like HH Remodeling LLC who can assess the condition and recommend the right timing for re-sealing to keep your logs healthy and beautiful.",
